
---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "@/components/nav.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="Hack The Box & TryHackMe Labs | Alfayo Robin">
  <Nav />

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-12 text-[var(--white)]">
    <a
      href="/#projects"
      class="mb-8 inline-block text-sm text-[var(--sec)] transition hover:opacity-80"
    >
      ← Back to Projects
    </a>

    <header class="mb-12">
      <p class="mb-3 text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[var(--sec)]">
        Cybersecurity • Continuous Learning
      </p>

      <h1 class="mb-5 text-3xl font-bold md:text-5xl">
        Hack The Box & TryHackMe Labs
      </h1>

      <p class="max-w-3xl text-base leading-7 opacity-80 md:text-lg">
        Hands-on cybersecurity learning through guided labs and practical
        exercises covering networking, Linux, Windows, web applications,
        reconnaissance, and vulnerability assessment.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <span class="rounded-full border border-white/20 px-3 py-1 text-sm">Hack The Box</span>
        <span class="rounded-full border border-white/20 px-3 py-1 text-sm">TryHackMe</span>
        <span class="rounded-full border border-white/20 px-3 py-1 text-sm">Linux</span>
        <span class="rounded-full border border-white/20 px-3 py-1 text-sm">Networking</span>
        <span class="rounded-full border border-white/20 px-3 py-1 text-sm">Reconnaissance</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">1. Overview</h2>
      <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
        I use Hack The Box Academy and TryHackMe to strengthen my cybersecurity
        knowledge through structured learning and practical exercises. The
        activities help me understand how systems communicate, how services
        can be investigated, and how security weaknesses may be identified.
        I document key commands, observations, challenges, and lessons learned
        as I progress.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="mb-6 text-2xl font-semibold">2. Hack The Box</h2>

      <div class="space-y-5">
        <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Linux Fundamentals</h3>
          <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
            Practised navigating the Linux command line and explored files,
            directories, permissions, processes, services, and basic networking
            commands. This provides a foundation for working with Linux systems
            during investigations and troubleshooting.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-70">
            Skills: Linux CLI, file permissions, processes, networking basics.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Windows Fundamentals</h3>
          <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
            Studied Windows system components, common administration features,
            and tools used to inspect and manage a Windows environment.
            These concepts are relevant to endpoint support and security monitoring.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-70">
            Skills: Windows administration concepts, system tools, troubleshooting.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Getting Started</h3>
          <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
            Explored foundational penetration-testing concepts, common security
            tools, reconnaissance, and the general process of assessing a
            target in a controlled training environment.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-70">
            Skills: Security methodology, enumeration concepts, command-line tools.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Introduction to Networking</h3>
          <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
            Studied networking concepts such as IP addressing, subnetting,
            protocols, DNS, and how devices communicate. These topics support
            troubleshooting and understanding network activity.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-70">
            Skills: TCP/IP, addressing, subnetting, protocols, DNS.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Web Fundamentals</h3>
          <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
            Learned about web applications, client-server communication,
            front-end and back-end components, databases, and web enumeration.
            This helps build an understanding of how web applications work and
            where security issues can arise.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-70">
            Skills: HTTP concepts, web architecture, application enumeration.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Vulnerability Assessment</h3>
          <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
            Studied vulnerability assessment concepts and explored tools such
            as Nessus. The module introduced how systems can be assessed for
            known weaknesses and why findings need to be reviewed and prioritised.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-70">
            Skills: Vulnerability scanning concepts, Nessus, findings review.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="mb-6 text-2xl font-semibold">3. TryHackMe</h2>

      <div class="space-y-5">
        <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Python Basics</h3>
          <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
            Worked through introductory Python concepts, including basic
            syntax, variables, data types, and simple programming logic.
            Python is useful for scripting repetitive tasks and supporting
            cybersecurity analysis.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-70">
            Skills: Python fundamentals, problem-solving, basic scripting.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Passive Reconnaissance</h3>
          <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
            Studied how publicly available information can be gathered about
            a target without directly interacting with its systems. This
            introduced information sources and techniques used during the
            reconnaissance stage of security assessments.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-70">
            Skills: OSINT concepts, information gathering, reconnaissance.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Threat Intelligence Tools</h3>
          <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
            Explored how threat intelligence resources can help investigate
            indicators and understand potential malicious activity. This
            supports the wider process of collecting context before making
            security decisions.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-70">
            Skills: Threat intelligence concepts, indicator research, analysis.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">4. Evidence and Documentation</h2>
      <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
        I maintain notes on the modules I study, including relevant commands,
        their purpose, important outputs, challenges, and what I learned from
        each exercise. Screenshots can be added to demonstrate completed
        activities and key findings.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <figure class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-4">
          <div class="flex min-h-36 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-white/5 p-6 text-center">
            <p class="text-sm opacity-60">Add a Hack The Box screenshot</p>
          </div>
          <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-75">
            Example: a completed module or terminal output from a lab.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <figure class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-4">
          <div class="flex min-h-36 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-white/5 p-6 text-center">
            <p class="text-sm opacity-60">Add a TryHackMe screenshot</p>
          </div>
          <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-75">
            Example: a completed room or evidence of a learning exercise.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">5. Challenges and Lessons Learned</h2>
      <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
        Some exercises required additional research to understand unfamiliar
        commands, interpret output, and work through configuration issues.
        Reviewing documentation and practising the concepts helped reinforce
        my understanding. The experience has also shown me the importance of
        taking clear notes, verifying results, and explaining technical
        findings in simple language.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-6">
      <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold">6. Conclusion</h2>
      <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
        These labs are helping me build a foundation in networking, operating
        systems, reconnaissance, vulnerability assessment, and security
        analysis. I intend to continue practising, documenting my results, and
        applying what I learn to my home lab and cybersecurity development.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
